    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a read-only `checkDigit` field = a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`. Since `checkDigit` is a pure derived value (like `membershipNumber` and `identityKey`), I added it as a mapper-computed field rather than persisting it:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (`type: integer`, `0\u20139`, `readOnly`), which drives generation of the `OwnerDto` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (skipping the non-digit separators like `SYD-SMI-0007`), returning `null` when the code is absent.\n\nThe test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts it matches `checkDigit` \u2014 it passes.",
